'' --help LISTS THE TARGETS, and the list is where a reader learns what -target takes.
'' TARGET_WIN32 and TARGET_WIN64 joined it on 2026-11-08; until then the line named the
'' three 64-bit targets and the test asserted exactly that.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --help
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: usage: tiko [options] <inputs...>
'' EXPECT-OUT: Subcommands:
'' EXPECT-OUT: tiko build    build the targets of tiko.toml
'' EXPECT-OUT: windows-x86_64 (the Windows default), win64, win32, linux-x86_64 or macos-arm64
'' EXPECT-NOT: RESUME support
'' EXPECT-OUT: Diagnostics:
'' EXPECT-OUT: --diagnostics-file <path>
'' EXPECT-OUT: Compiler development:
